                      (../MS Extended BA):03898         ; EXP ( E**X)                      
                      (../MS Extended BA):03899         ; THE EXPONENTIAL FUNCTION IS EVALUATED BY FIRST MULTIPLYING THE                      
                      (../MS Extended BA):03900         ; ARGUMENT BY A CORRECTION FACTOR (CF). AFTER THIS IS DONE, AN                      
                      (../MS Extended BA):03901         ; ARGUMENT >= 127 WILL YIELD A ZERO RESULT (NO UNDERFLOW) FOR A                      
                      (../MS Extended BA):03902         ; NEGATIVE ARGUMENT OR AN 'OV' (OVERFLOW) ERROR FOR A POSITIVE                      
                      (../MS Extended BA):03903         ; ARGUMENT. THE POLYNOMIAL COEFFICIENTS ARE MODIFIED TO REFLECT                      
                      (../MS Extended BA):03904         ; THE CF MULTIPLICATION AT THE START OF THE EVALUATION PROCESS.                      
                      (../MS Extended BA):03905                                        
